        "timing": { "kind": "not-specified-by-source" }
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "Fleischner recommends, for a solitary, solid, incidental pulmonary nodule greater than 8mm and up to 30mm in diameter (Fleischner's own nodule/mass boundary), in a patient >=35 years old with no known malignancy history and not immunocompromised: CT surveillance at 3 months, or further characterization by PET-CT, or biopsy/tissue sampling -- presented as coequal options with no source-stated ranking between them."
